#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "a30b523c-d689-520a-a708-f3b5190eaf9d" :question/math-academy-id "e-477" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad  \\cos^2 x = 1-\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096468 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "872b9d99-ea39-540f-af2e-acbfa28186b4" :question/math-academy-id "e-478" :question/problem "Calculate $\\, \\displaystyle{\\int} \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\tan^2{x}$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2x =\\sec^2x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x =\\sec^2 x -1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\tan x -x+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096469 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "d7c09fca-2f4b-5a0a-b687-938527b44d62" :question/math-academy-id "e-479" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+\\cot^2x =\\csc^2 x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\cot^2 x &=\\csc^2 x -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\bigg(5\\left(\\csc^2 x -1 \\right) -x^2\\bigg) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\int \\left(5\\csc^2 x -5 -x^2\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=-5\\cot x -5x-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096470 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/id #uuid "14ab2251-66fc-5f94-9821-f14fcc2c03e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-480" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d} x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity  $1+\\tan^2 \\theta =\\sec^2 \\theta$ with $\\theta = 3x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t1+\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x)\\\n\t\t\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x) -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x&= 2\\int \\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                &= 2\\int \\left(\\sec^2 (3x) -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                 &= 2\\left(\\int \\sec^2 (3x)\\, \\textrm{d}x -\\int1 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t                                &= 2\\left( \\dfrac{1}{3}\\tan (3x) -x\\right)+C\\\n                                                                 &= \t\\dfrac{2}{3}\\tan (3x) -2x+C.\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b7b03d-566b-57ff-9b57-89245c891150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247450} {:answer/id #uuid "258d518c-1393-51c3-9f47-dac610e236f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247755} {:answer/id #uuid "6da8f4fb-e78a-5608-aaf9-5f82ea791cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248397} {:answer/id #uuid "6e400284-d57a-58fe-928b-40d3a6d7f47d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248400} {:answer/id #uuid "772c83ac-213f-55d7-9be6-27ef7871587f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "772c83ac-213f-55d7-9be6-27ef7871587f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248473} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e185e9d-354f-5cb8-8cd3-194e9a76c8b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47d60902-14e4-57db-9a3c-83c4f5318199" :question/math-academy-id "q-114435" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+{tan}^{2}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{cos}^{3}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250274 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "429c4e06-3048-55b1-b208-72019f1b0474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248017} {:answer/id #uuid "7e54eb59-7b2b-5295-a85f-69bab12eefd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248535} {:answer/id #uuid "8021e056-c15c-5db2-b077-c41b6d899f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248549} {:answer/id #uuid "848e9fc1-831c-51f0-9f79-1b100b19ee3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248600} {:answer/id #uuid "b94c2031-9662-5675-9f0a-6203b77aab15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e54eb59-7b2b-5295-a85f-69bab12eefd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248535} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0cd4974-971c-56d8-b46a-a70cd95372ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a520c33d-1aa5-5864-8fa9-daf66894b11e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114469" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1+{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sec}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ with $\\theta =2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})={sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{[{tan}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+1]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})}\\,\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\text{d}x & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+\\frac{\\pi }{5})+C & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3664de6-d101-5f3f-b8ae-800b29d566b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3664de6-d101-5f3f-b8ae-800b29d566b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318126} :answer-field/id #uuid "169f7f1d-db26-55ad-9330-bc1460e5358d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb1a86d3-f725-5234-baee-3e7bfe9e8077" :question/math-academy-id "q-346553" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }({cos}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64dedadd-0d5b-56a4-a48b-8d951ecd5865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-2\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64dedadd-0d5b-56a4-a48b-8d951ecd5865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-2\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319700} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e4fc3ea-da9e-59c7-a0e0-47d8251661de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5f1d4130-f1fa-520f-a18a-606ae77d72dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-352709" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}({cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}({cot}^{2}⁡x-{csc}^{2}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi /2}(2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-x)\\,{|}_{1}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =({(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-({1}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}-2\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bcde715-09f6-55d0-9e0a-cb7faecc72f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bcde715-09f6-55d0-9e0a-cb7faecc72f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319859} :answer-field/id #uuid "d949c466-9f8a-51dc-9620-89072bd789f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c03309dc-5937-5269-a513-e248a0216700" :question/math-academy-id "q-352747" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}[4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+3{x}^{2}+4{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)]\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the identity ${sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ with $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2}-1,$ we get \n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+3{x}^{2}+4{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)]\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[3{x}^{2}+4({sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1)+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}-1))]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3{x}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}+4x]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[{1}^{3}+4(1)]-[{0}^{3}+4(0)] \\\\  & =5-0 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323773 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fa96cf1-4d31-5deb-b3f4-3a3294848a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fa96cf1-4d31-5deb-b3f4-3a3294848a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321270} :answer-field/id #uuid "17fe46a9-616b-5b04-b80d-53e10861f0fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39b5bd8a-dd36-5527-89de-e36f567f0906" :question/math-academy-id "q-362509" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwe compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89a639e1-ea30-5852-945d-838c01f3a530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89a639e1-ea30-5852-945d-838c01f3a530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322245} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfbc300f-8435-5b63-80a7-df2fbc495791" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a3e4c61-3446-503d-9221-974875074079" :question/math-academy-id "q-362530" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{4}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1-{cot}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7841411-b2a3-5f14-a4fa-569475a21ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7841411-b2a3-5f14-a4fa-569475a21ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323091} :answer-field/id #uuid "274f1f5a-362f-555e-b4c6-9b261c2ad7ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "053d1129-5ad9-5392-8059-7eab09c97e80" :question/math-academy-id "q-362804" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{csc}^{4}⁡x-1}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity\n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{csc}^{4}⁡x-1}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)({csc}^{2}⁡x+1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}({csc}^{2}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {cot}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008298da-bf7a-51ca-837d-ab329d0489ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329955} {:answer/id #uuid "099d6ddf-d5f2-5fd1-9989-6721d1ea7bce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330034} {:answer/id #uuid "88ac8b32-2829-5bde-aed3-69f279dfedfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331164} {:answer/id #uuid "97b2c286-d293-598e-8173-52cb4aaa72e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331301} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c3c459-f04c-5677-8215-e3b74b9824f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2c3c459-f04c-5677-8215-e3b74b9824f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331681} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2910a34-30ac-5541-b445-de1db206308c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d70cb193-c0f3-511e-a986-3ca7b8cef3f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-49332" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{1-{cot}^{4}⁡x}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{1-{cot}^{4}⁡x}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096830 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0860c1d8-216d-5466-9f62-ccae7b52e912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330020} {:answer/id #uuid "203a6ea8-eba0-5d40-aa09-a59a360ffbdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330226} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb98399-a9d4-5fe9-bc96-644e80f830a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330488} {:answer/id #uuid "823db0e7-2377-5017-b419-f145d5d9961d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331099} {:answer/id #uuid "8a3e9f10-f5ea-57a0-9d29-03b20270bd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a3e9f10-f5ea-57a0-9d29-03b20270bd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331177} :answer-field/id #uuid "a10a89c1-f082-55be-bb60-453abc8e5020" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "71ebda71-dbd6-53ac-9e9c-22ae8c3a8413" :question/math-academy-id "q-49446" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.$ \nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}=\\frac{1}{-{sin}^{2}⁡x}=-{csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
